WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.551
Apollo Q Labs. Level one, module three: buying, selling, and implied volatility.

2
00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:16.919
Every option trade has two sides: the buyer, who is long, meaning you bought it, and the seller, who is short, meaning you sold it and carry the obligation.

3
00:00:16.919 --> 00:00:22.125
The buyer pays the premium, the price of an option. Risk is limited to that premium.

4
00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:29.316
The buyer needs the stock to move enough, soon enough. Time decay, the loss of value as time passes, works against you.

5
00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:33.691
The seller collects the premium up front. Profit is capped at that premium.

6
00:00:33.691 --> 00:00:43.121
Time decay works for the seller. But you can be assigned, meaning made to buy or sell the shares, and some short positions have large or unlimited risk.

7
00:00:43.421 --> 00:00:46.388
Next: implied volatility, or I V.

8
00:00:46.388 --> 00:00:50.357
I V is the expected yearly move priced into options.

9
00:00:50.357 --> 00:01:01.985
High I V makes options expensive, which favors sellers. Low I V makes them cheap, which favors buyers. That is a rule of thumb. It does not tell you which trade to take.

10
00:01:02.285 --> 00:01:12.975
A rough one standard deviation move, meaning a typical size move, over D days, is price, times I V, times the square root of D divided by three sixty five.

11
00:01:12.975 --> 00:01:17.605
Take a one hundred dollar stock, with thirty percent I V, over thirty days.

12
00:01:17.605 --> 00:01:25.244
One hundred times point three, times the square root of thirty over three sixty five, is about eight dollars and sixty cents.

13
00:01:25.244 --> 00:01:36.061
About two times out of three the stock ends within plus or minus eight dollars and sixty cents of today’s price. One time in three it goes further, so this is not a limit.

14
00:01:36.361 --> 00:01:43.509
I V often rises before events like earnings, a company’s results report, and drops right after.

15
00:01:43.809 --> 00:01:56.547
Recap: buyers risk only the premium, sellers collect it but can face large risk, and high I V favors sellers and low I V favors buyers, a rule of thumb, not a signal for which trade to take.

16
00:01:56.547 --> 00:02:00.153
Next, read the lessons, then take the six question quiz.

